<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Daewon Sanup withdraws listing plan.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Daewon Sanup withdraws listing plan.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Daewon Sanup Co Ltd, an automobile part producer, has withdrawn its initial public offering (IPO) plan, the Securities Supervisory Board (SSB) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>A company official said the cancellation of the listing plan was due to worsening prospects of earnings this year as a result of a slowdown in the car industry.</p>
<p>The SSB said it had requested Daewon to submit documents on depreciation and reserves for severance payments.</p>
<p>The company was expected to be listed in July.</p>
</text>
